quran[16]{c,v,t}:
  38,1,"Sad. By the Qur’an, full of Reminder."
  38,2,(This is the truth) but the disbelievers are steeped in arrogance and opposition.
  38,3,How many generations have We destroyed before them? And they called out for help when the time for escape had passed.
  38,4,"They think it strange that a warner has come to them from among themselves. So the disbelievers say: ‘This is a magician, a great liar."
  38,5,"Has he reduced the gods to one God? Indeed, this is something extremely astonishing!’"
  38,6,"The leaders among them (i.e. the Quraysh) departed (saying): ‘Walk away and stand firm to your gods! Indeed, this is something designed (to usurp power)."
  38,7,We did not hear any such claim in the last religion. It is nothing but a fabrication.
  38,8,"Has the Reminder been revealed (only) to him among us (all)?’ Instead, they are in doubt regarding My Reminder. Nay! They have not yet tasted My punishment."
  38,9,"Do they possess the treasures of your Lord’s mercy—the All-Mighty, the Great Bestower?"
  38,10,"Or do they own the kingdom of the heavens, the earth and whatever is between them? (If so,) then let them ascend (into the heavens) by some means."
  38,11,(They are just) an army bound to be crushed from among the factions.
  38,12,"Before them, the people of Nuh (Noah) and ‘Ad denied (their messengers), and (so did) Pharaoh, who used to impale (his victims)."
  38,13,And (so did) Thamud and the people of Lut (Lot) and the Forest-dwellers (i.e. the people of Shu‘ayb). These were all confederates (against the truth).
  38,14,"Each of them denied the messengers. So, My retribution (against them) became due."
  38,15,All these (disbelievers) are waiting just for a single blast that will not be postponed (for a while).
  38,16,And they say (mockingly): ‘Our Lord! Hasten for us our share before the Day of Reckoning.’
